\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Shared links and periodic face labels}
\date{2026-11-11}

\p{In the [sign-valued torus calculation](fdip-006Q), a
chosen edge occurs in the boundaries of neighboring oriented
faces. A periodic cubic lattice has the same shared-edge
incidences in several coordinate planes. The Fourier
expansion of \ref{fdip-00NJ} assigns a label in
#{\mathbb Z/N} to each face, and the original link sum
contains the character factors from every incident face.
Which labelings survive the sum over a shared link, and how
can their winding around the periodic directions be recorded?}
